From 771ae9fdc8754ae68dc1713cc26b853184011ab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:06:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mcp): trim the user-settings-update response like
 user-get

user-get returns a trimmed profile: the nested organization and project
objects keep only id and name, and impersonation state is left out.
user-settings-update returned the raw PATCH body instead, so any settings
change echoed every organization project, each with its API token, which
project-get is documented as the only tool to return.

The update tool now declares the same response fields as user-get. The
generated handler is edited by hand to match what the generator emits for
user-get, because codegen needs the backend OpenAPI schema.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
